 34AR  H TYP=FUL$AUT=LIJIE SUN AND JUN CHEN$CIT=ENSDF$CUT=30-Sep-2026$          
 34AR c  2020Ke03: E=95 MeV {+24}Mg beam was produced from the ATLAS accelerator
 34AR2c  at ANL. Target was |?200 |mg/cm{+2} {+12}C. |g rays were detected with 
 34AR3c  the GRETINA tracking array consisting of 12 modules; recoils were      
 34AR4c  separated and identified by the Fragment Mass Analyzer (FMA) with a    
 34AR5c  position-sensitive parallel-grid avalanche counter (PGAC) and an       
 34AR6c  ionization chamber. Measured E|g, I|g, |g|g-coin, particle-|g-coin.    
 34AR7c  Deduced levels, J, |p, proton-resonance energy. Discussed implications 
 34AR8c  for astrophysical {+33}Cl(p,|g) reaction rate.                         
